## Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project using the latest official documentation.

### Changes Made:

**1. Package Installation:**
   - Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
   - Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
   - Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the installation

**2. Code Integration:**
   - Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to include Vercel Analytics
   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the Auth0Provider
   - Followed Next.js App Router integration pattern as specified in official docs

### Implementation Details:

The Analytics component was added to the root layout following the App Router pattern from the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart). The component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't interfere with existing functionality while still tracking all page views and visitor data.

The integration preserves all existing code structure including:
- Auth0 authentication provider
- Metadata configuration
- Main layout structure
- Global CSS imports

### Next Steps:

To activate Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
2. Deploy the changes to production using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify tracking is active by checking the browser Network tab for analytics requests

### Verification:

- ✅ Package successfully installed and can be imported
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passes for the modified layout file (no new errors introduced)
- ✅ Code follows Next.js App Router best practices
- ✅ Existing functionality preserved (Auth0Provider, metadata, etc.)

### Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

Note: Pre-existing build issues related to Prisma configuration were identified but are unrelated to this Analytics integration. The Analytics component itself is properly configured and ready for deployment.
